# EmailJS configuration is NOT read from the environment.
#
# The service ID, both template IDs, and the (browser-visible) public key are
# defined in src/config/emailjs.ts so the static site builds without any host
# or CI configuration. See docs/EMAILJS_SETUP.md.
#
# Do not add EmailJS values here: nothing reads them any more, and a stale
# value would silently disagree with the code. Never put private API keys,
# Microsoft 365 credentials, OAuth tokens, or recipient/BCC addresses in any
# VITE_* variable — everything with a VITE_ prefix is compiled into the public
# browser bundle.
#
# The one build-time switch that exists is for the automated checks only and
# must never be set for a real build:
#   VITE_EMAILJS_FORCE_UNCONFIGURED=true

# Optional future server-side lead endpoint (unrelated to the EmailJS form).
VITE_LEAD_FORM_ENDPOINT=
